# Loaded automatically by `vite build` (mode=production) and baked into the
# bundle at build time. This file exists because a production build with NO
# value anywhere silently compiles `buildEnv("VITE_ACCOUNTS_API")` to "" —
# "same origin as this page" — and the desktop shell's 4410 API serves no
# /v1/auth routes, so the HUAWEI sign-in button navigated the main window to
# a path the static SPA fallback answered with index.html: the page reloaded
# onto the sign-in screen in a tight loop that looked like a crash (W27,
# observed on a 2026-11-27 install where the button did this 78 times).
#
# Override precedence (vite): real environment variables > this file, so CI or
# a local experiment can point the bundle at another deployment with
# `VITE_ACCOUNTS_API=... pnpm build` without editing anything. Dev
# (`vite` → mode=development) never loads this file — see .env.example for
# the dev story.
VITE_ACCOUNTS_API=https://sciencediscovery.openjiuwen.com/accounts
